abstract: >
  HERESY v5.0.0 is a 5,424-byte native Commodore 64 desktop built around a
  326-byte cooperative 6510 microkernel. Eleven services communicate through
  32 fixed eight-byte records and receive memory from sixteen brokered pages.
  Files, Notes, Calculator and System provide practical offline functions;
  Notes uses a recoverable 1541 scratch/write/scratch/rename transaction. The
  FORCEOS '38 demoscene application uses real VIC-II raster effects and SID
  audio to satirise infrastructure bloat and tool-as-religion thinking.
